            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdominal condition caused by retrograde bleeding in a postmenopausal patient on estrogen-progestogen therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>677-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Retrograde blood flow in menstruating women has been described recently. The acute event seems to be asymptomatic. Reported here is a case of an acute abdominal condition due to cervical obstruction and retrograde bleeding in a postmenopausal patient treated with estrogen-progestogen therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
